{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","externalID":"s:s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"role":"symbol","title":"ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral","symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Collection-Literals","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"],"title":"Collection Literals"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A dictionary literal is a simple way of writing a list of key-value pairs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You write each key-value pair with a colon (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":":"},{"text":") separating the key and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the value. The dictionary literal is made up of one or more key-value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pairs, separated by commas and surrounded with square brackets.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To declare a dictionary, assign a dictionary literal to a variable or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constant:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let countryCodes = [\"BR\": \"Brazil\", \"GH\": \"Ghana\",","                    \"JP\": \"Japan\", \"US\": \"United States\"]","\/\/ 'countryCodes' has type '[String: String]'","","print(countryCodes[\"BR\"]!)","\/\/ Prints \"Brazil\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the context provides enough type information, you can use a special","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"form of the dictionary literal, square brackets surrounding a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colon, to initialize an empty dictionary.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var frequencies: [String: Int] = [:]","print(frequencies.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\""]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary literal is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the same as an instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can’t initialize a type that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simply by assigning an instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValuePairs"},{"type":"text","text":", or similar."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"anchor":"Conforming-to-the-ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral-Protocol","type":"heading","level":1,"text":"Conforming to the ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral Protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To add the capability to be initialized with a dictionary literal to your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own custom types, declare an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(dictionaryLiteral:)"},{"text":" initializer. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following example shows the dictionary literal initializer for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hypothetical ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CountedSet"},{"text":" type, which uses setlike semantics while keeping","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"track of the count for duplicate elements:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct CountedSet<Element: Hashable>: Collection, SetAlgebra {","    \/\/ implementation details","","    \/\/\/ Updates the count stored in the set for the given element,","    \/\/\/ adding the element if necessary.","    \/\/\/","    \/\/\/ - Parameter n: The new count for `element`. `n` must be greater","    \/\/\/   than or equal to zero.","    \/\/\/ - Parameter element: The element to set the new count on.","    mutating func updateCount(_ n: Int, for element: Element)","}","","extension CountedSet: ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral {","    init(dictionaryLiteral elements: (Element, Int)...) {","        self.init()","        for (element, count) in elements {","            self.updateCount(count, for: element)","        }","    }","}"]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritedBy","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Cxx\/CxxDictionary"],"title":"Inherited By"},{"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.S